 attached.\nL177: That split is the story of this page: same model, wildly different results depending on the hardware and the serving recipe.\nL178: ## Where it runs best\nL179: \nL180: Our measurements cover four hardware families, and the honest ranking is clear.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen3.8-Flash-Next Benchmarks: Measured Speed | Petronella (https://petronellatech.com/ai/llm-benchmarks/models/qwen3-8-flash-next/)\nciteturn4view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://petronellatech.com/ai/llm-benchmarks/models/qwen3-8-flash-next/\",\"lineno\":120}); Total lines: 363\nL64: Engine  | vLLM, vLLM nightly, oxbyte MTP4, EP, vLLM, oxbyte MTP4, EP, Gufo 0.12.0 (ROCm), Gufo 0.12.0 (ROCm), no MTP, unsloth llama.cpp b11505-mix (ROCm), MTP 3, unsloth llama.cpp b11505-mix (Vulkan RADV), MTP 3, unsloth llama.cpp b11505-mix (Vulkan RADV), no MTP, llama.cpp Vulkan (Windows), MTP 3, llama.cpp Vulkan (Windows), no MTP\nL65: Quantization  | NVFP4 (RadixArk checkpoint, bf16 KV), NVFP4, UD-Q4_K_XL\nL66: Best single-user speed  | 205 tok/s\nL67: Best aggregate (8 users)  | not measured\nL68: Verified context  | 243,392 tokens\nL69: The fastest single-user prose speed we measured for this model is 205 tokens per second.\nL70: ## Checked, not assumed\nL71: \nL72: Needle found at 243,392 tokens\nL73: \nL74: 1x GB300 · NVFP4 (RadixArk checkpoint, bf16 KV)\nL75: \nL76: 39k-token needle generation speed\nL77: \nL78: 1x ai11 · UD-Q4_K_XL · unsloth llama.cpp b11505-mix (Vulkan RADV), MTP 3\nL79: ## How speed holds up as users are added\nL80: \nL81: Configuration  | 1 user  | 32 users  | At ceiling\nL82: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL83: 1x GB300 · NVFP4 (RadixArk checkpoint, bf16 KV)  | 205 tok/s  | 3,007 tok/s  |\nL84: 2x GB10, TP2 · NVFP4  | 35.2 tok/s  | 329.6 tok/s  | 329.6 tok/s at 32 users\nL85: 4x GB10, TP4 · NVFP4  | 41.4 tok/s  | 482.4 tok/s  | 648.7 tok/s at 64 users\nL86: